Expected elements: present

I checked each required item individually and every one is there. Provenance banner: first in the shell, above the identity bar, badge "Synthetic demo data", chain slug `aztec`, three producer sentences whose tone matches the label. Identity bar: `← aztec` (exit targeting the chain, correct), `0xb63616…6359`, `Partial`, `block 101`, both stepping directions plus step-in/out, a scrubber, the readout `128 / 1315`, the phase rail FETCHING/OPENING/POSITIONING, and a NOIR tag. Code pane titled CODE with line 32 marked at the pinned coordinate. CALL TRACE and EVENT LOG as one tab strip with CALL TRACE open, seven frames, holding the larger share of its column. VALUES a separate pane below the strip, ten values. TRANSACTION metadata pane. No spinner, no empty pane, no light chrome, no full-width prose band below the bar, no full-width pane row, Values not in the tab strip.

In register terms this is convincingly the desktop tool: dark, dense, mono-textured, and the copy is specific and unapologetic throughout. Three crossings back toward the explorer voice weaken it: the banner's marketing-grade prose setting, the oversized annotation paragraphs in the TRANSACTION pane, and half of the CALL TRACE region reading as void.

Highest-priority fixes: reset the provenance banner's type to debugger density so it costs ~90 rows instead of ~180, and give the call trace region's dead height back to Code.

Rating: 7/10

